WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.120
Our running case is a dense accelerator deployment with liquid cooling, constrained

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.340
site access and a requirement to grow.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.220
It is a teaching scenario, not a specification for a real installation.

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.280
The team has a rack proposal and several attractive component ratings, but

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.100
hasn't yet demonstrated that the complete configuration meets its operating envelope.

6
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.740
Start an evidence record with five headings: mechanical and payload, power, thermal,

7
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.340
site route, and service and control.

8
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:32.259
For each, record the requirement, proposed solution, supporting evidence and unresolved issue.

9
00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:36.060
An unresolved issue needs an owner and a closure condition, not a

10
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.820
vague assurance that it will be handled later.

11
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.800
At each stage we'll choose go, conditional go or hold.

12
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.440
Conditional go means a bounded next activity is permitted with explicit restrictions;

13
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.620
it doesn't mean commissioning is approved.

14
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.580
Hold means a missing or conflicting item blocks the requested activity.

15
00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.200
Pause and identify one question you'd ask under each heading.

16
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.360
We'll refine those questions as the interfaces and failure cases become concrete.

